[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Start "two-knights-d3 4.d3"]
[Name "Two Knights: the modest ...Be7"]

4... Be7 { A safe square, but a modest one: the bishop does not aim at f2, so White has time for everything. }
5. c3 { The usual plan, with d4 in mind. [%cal Gc3d4] }
5... O-O 6. O-O d6 7. Re1 { Guards e4 a second time and frees the knight on f3. }
7... Bg4 { The pin again, the band's most common move here. [%icon pin@f3] }
8. h3 { Asks the bishop to decide. }
8... Bh5 9. Nbd2 { The same answer as in the Giuoco Piano: the knight guards f3 and heads for f1 and g3, where it will chase the bishop. [%cal Gd2f1,Gf1g3] } *
